# Educational Video Automation Contract

- Treat source PDF/extracted text as the factual authority; preserve provenance to page/section.
- Use `educational-video` for new PDF chapters and follow its declared stage order.
- Initialize a project workspace and write `in_progress` checkpoints before long stages.
- Never bypass a manifest human gate. Stop after writing `awaiting_human`.
- Use measured narration duration as the authoritative timeline; apply title offsets once.
- Run `hybrid_asset_router` before selecting or generating final visuals and record every scene decision.
- Run subject-aware media research first; stock-search results are candidates until visually reviewed.
- Prefer reviewed project assets, then licensed stock for factual subjects.
- Use generated video only for justified continuity/specificity gaps and within approved budget.
- Never silently switch provider, model, runtime, or stock/generated treatment.
- The user's selected educational-video composition runtime is HyperFrames. Preserve it unless a project-specific blocker is surfaced and a new runtime decision is approved.
- Record license, source URL, provider/model, prompt, seed, cost, and scene mapping.
- Validate artifacts against schemas before checkpointing.
- Do not publish unless encoded-video QA and `final_review.status == "pass"`.
- Destructive filesystem changes, paid calls above policy, publishing, and external messages require approval.
- Keep every output under `projects/<project-id>/`; preserve prior versions and checkpoint history.
